IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ea-core`
IMPORT `ea-definitions`
IMPORT `ea1-part2b-continuity`

-- Tests for ea1-part2b-continuity.l4 (ss 18 to 19).  Every expected value is written
-- from the text of the section (inputs/EmA1968.txt) before the function was run.

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§ `s 18 Change of employer`
-- (1): arguments are: the contract between a body corporate and an employee is modified by or under a written law, another body corporate is substituted.
#ASSERT `s 18(1) the employee's period of employment counts as a period of employment with the other body corporate` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 18(1) the employee's period of employment counts as a period of employment with the other body corporate` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 18(1) "If by or under any written law ...": a change of employer that is not so brought about, or a substitution that did not happen, is an unmet "if": no (ruled 2026-11-05 (b)).
#ASSERT `s 18(1) the employee's period of employment counts as a period of employment with the other body corporate` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- "the change of employer does not break the continuity": the answer to "does it break" is no.
#ASSERT `s 18(1) the change of employer breaks the continuity of the period of employment` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 18(1) the change of employer breaks the continuity of the period of employment` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (2): the employer has died, the employee is taken into the employment of the personal representatives or trustees.
#ASSERT `s 18(2) the employee's period of employment counts as a period of employment with the employer's personal representatives or trustees` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 18(2) the employee's period of employment counts as a period of employment with the employer's personal representatives or trustees` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 18(2) the employee's period of employment counts as a period of employment with the employer's personal representatives or trustees` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 18(2) the death of the employer breaks the continuity of the period of employment` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 18(2) the death of the employer breaks the continuity of the period of employment` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (3)
#ASSERT `s 18(3) the employee's period of employment counts as a period of employment with the partners, personal representatives or trustees after the change` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 18(3) the employee's period of employment counts as a period of employment with the partners, personal representatives or trustees after the change` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 18(3) the change breaks the continuity of the period of employment` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 18(3) the change breaks the continuity of the period of employment` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§ `s 18A Transfer of employment`
-- (1)(a), (1)(b): arguments are: an undertaking or part is transferred, the person was employed by the transferor in it.
#ASSERT `s 18A(1)(a) the transfer operates to terminate the contract of service of the person employed` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 18A(1)(a) the transfer operates to terminate the contract of service of the person employed` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 18A(1)(a) the transfer operates to terminate the contract of service of the person employed` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 18A(1)(a) the contract of service has effect after the transfer as if originally made between the person employed and the transferee` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 18A(1)(a) the contract of service has effect after the transfer as if originally made between the person employed and the transferee` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 18A(1)(b) the period of employment of the employee counts as a period of employment with the transferee` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 18A(1)(b) the period of employment of the employee counts as a period of employment with the transferee` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 18A(1)(b) the transfer breaks the continuity of the period of employment` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 18A(1)(b) the transfer breaks the continuity of the period of employment` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (2)(a), (b), (c)
#ASSERT `s 18A(2)(a) the transferor's right, power, duty or liability is transferred to the transferee` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 18A(2) "on completion of a transfer": no completed transfer, no transfer of rights by this subsection ("on completion of" read as "upon": fork F-EVENT).
#ASSERT `s 18A(2)(a) the transferor's right, power, duty or liability is transferred to the transferee` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 18A(2)(a) the transferor's right, power, duty or liability is transferred to the transferee` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 18A(2)(b) the act or omission is deemed to have been done by the transferee` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 18A(2)(b) the act or omission is deemed to have been done by the transferee` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 18A(2)(c) the act or omission is deemed to have been done in relation to the transferee` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 18A(2)(c) the act or omission is deemed to have been done in relation to the transferee` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (3)
#ASSERT `s 18A(3) the terms and conditions of service are the same as those enjoyed immediately prior to the transfer` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 18A(3) the terms and conditions of service are the same as those enjoyed immediately prior to the transfer` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (4): "do not transfer or otherwise affect the liability to be prosecuted".
#ASSERT `s 18A(4) subsections (1) and (2) transfer or otherwise affect the liability` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 18A(4) subsections (1) and (2) transfer or otherwise affect the liability` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (5)
#ASSERT `s 18A(5) the transferor must notify the affected employees and the trade union of affected employees (if any) of the matters` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 18A(5) the transferor must notify the affected employees and the trade union of affected employees (if any) of the matters` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- notified on 1 June for a transfer on 1 July, as soon as reasonable: in time.
#ASSERT `s 18A(5) the transferor notified as soon as it was reasonable and before the transfer took place` (Date 1 6 2026) (Date 1 7 2026) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- notified on the day of the transfer: not "before".
#ASSERT `s 18A(5) the transferor notified as soon as it was reasonable and before the transfer took place` (Date 1 7 2026) (Date 1 7 2026) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 18A(5) the transferor notified as soon as it was reasonable and before the transfer took place` (Date 30 6 2026) (Date 1 7 2026) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- before the transfer but not as soon as it was reasonable.
#ASSERT `s 18A(5) the transferor notified as soon as it was reasonable and before the transfer took place` (Date 30 6 2026) (Date 1 7 2026) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (a), (b), (c): all three matters.
#ASSERT `s 18A(5)(a), (b) and (c) the notification is of all the matters` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 18A(5)(a), (b) and (c) the notification is of all the matters` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 18A(5)(a), (b) and (c) the notification is of all the matters` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- the duty as a regulative rule: a transfer in 30 days; notifying at day 10 fulfils, at day 30 breaches (read both traces).
#TRACE `s 18A(5) the transferor's duty to notify` 30 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 18A(5) the transferor` DOES `s 18A(5) notify the affected employees and the trade union of affected employees of the matters in paragraphs (a), (b) and (c)` AT 10
#TRACE `s 18A(5) the transferor's duty to notify` 30 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 18A(5) the transferor` DOES `s 18A(5) notify the affected employees and the trade union of affected employees of the matters in paragraphs (a), (b) and (c)` AT 30
-- (6), (7)
#ASSERT `s 18A(6) the transferee must give the transferor the information` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 18A(6) the transferee must give the transferor the information` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 18A(7)(a) the Commissioner may, by written notice, direct the transferor to comply with subsection (5) within the time specified in the notice` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 18A(7): "Where the Commissioner considers that there has been an inordinate delay" not met: no.
#ASSERT `s 18A(7)(a) the Commissioner may, by written notice, direct the transferor to comply with subsection (5) within the time specified in the notice` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 18A(7)(b) the Commissioner may, by written notice, direct the transferee to comply with subsection (6) within the time specified in the notice` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 18A(7)(b) the Commissioner may, by written notice, direct the transferee to comply with subsection (6) within the time specified in the notice` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (8): arguments are: recognised by the transferor in respect of the employee, the employee becomes the transferee's employee, a majority of the transferee's employees are members.
#ASSERT `s 18A(8)(a) the trade union is deemed to be recognised by the transferee for the purposes of the Industrial Relations Act 1960` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 18A(8)(a) the trade union is deemed to be recognised by the transferee for the purposes of the Industrial Relations Act 1960` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 18A(8): the "Where" is unmet when the union was not recognised by the transferor, or the employee does not become the transferee's employee: no (ruled 2026-11-05 (b)).
#ASSERT `s 18A(8)(a) the trade union is deemed to be recognised by the transferee for the purposes of the Industrial Relations Act 1960` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 18A(8)(a) the trade union is deemed to be recognised by the transferee for the purposes of the Industrial Relations Act 1960` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (b): "in any other case": no majority; recognised only for disputes (i) and (ii).
#ASSERT `s 18A(8)(b) the trade union is deemed to be recognised by the transferee for the purpose of representing the employee on the dispute` TRUE TRUE FALSE `s 18A(8)(b)(i) a dispute from a collective agreement entered into between the transferor and the trade union while the collective agreement remains in force` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 18A(8)(b) the trade union is deemed to be recognised by the transferee for the purpose of representing the employee on the dispute` TRUE TRUE FALSE `s 18A(8)(b)(ii) a dispute from the transfer of the employee's employment from the transferor to the transferee` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 18A(8)(b) the trade union is deemed to be recognised by the transferee for the purpose of representing the employee on the dispute` TRUE TRUE FALSE `s 18A(8) a dispute from some other matter` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- where a majority are members, paragraph (a) applies, and (b) is silent.
#ASSERT `s 18A(8)(b) the trade union is deemed to be recognised by the transferee for the purpose of representing the employee on the dispute` TRUE TRUE TRUE `s 18A(8) a dispute from some other matter` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 18A(8)(b) the trade union is deemed to be recognised by the transferee for the purpose of representing the employee on the dispute` FALSE TRUE FALSE `s 18A(8)(b)(ii) a dispute from the transfer of the employee's employment from the transferor to the transferee` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (8A): the agreement continues 18 months after the day of the transfer, or to its expiry, whichever is the later.
#ASSERT `s 18A(8A) the last day on which the collective agreement continues in force between the transferee and the trade union` (Date 1 3 2026) NOTHING EQUALS Date 1 9 2027
-- expiry later than the 18 months: the expiry.
#ASSERT `s 18A(8A) the last day on which the collective agreement continues in force between the transferee and the trade union` (Date 1 3 2026) (JUST (Date 31 12 2027)) EQUALS Date 31 12 2027
-- expiry earlier than the 18 months: the 18 months.
#ASSERT `s 18A(8A) the last day on which the collective agreement continues in force between the transferee and the trade union` (Date 1 3 2026) (JUST (Date 31 8 2027)) EQUALS Date 1 9 2027
-- a transfer in late 2026: 18 months go into 2028.
#ASSERT `s 18A(8A) the last day on which the collective agreement continues in force between the transferee and the trade union` (Date 15 11 2026) NOTHING EQUALS Date 15 5 2028
-- (9), (10)
#ASSERT `s 18A(9) a party may refer the dispute to the Commissioner under section 115, and it is deemed to be a dispute to which that section applies` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 18A(9) a party may refer the dispute to the Commissioner under section 115, and it is deemed to be a dispute to which that section applies` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 18A(10)(a) the Commissioner has the power to delay or prohibit the transfer of employment of the employee` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 18A(10): "Where a dispute or disagreement has been referred to the Commissioner pursuant to subsection (9)" not met: no (ruled 2026-11-05 (b)).
#ASSERT `s 18A(10)(a) the Commissioner has the power to delay or prohibit the transfer of employment of the employee` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 18A(10)(b) the Commissioner has the power to order that the transfer of employment be subject to terms that the Commissioner considers just` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 18A(10)(b) the Commissioner has the power to order that the transfer of employment be subject to terms that the Commissioner considers just` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (12)
#ASSERT `s 18A(12) the parties may negotiate for and agree to terms of service different from those of the preserved contract of service` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 18A(12) the parties may negotiate for and agree to terms of service different from those of the preserved contract of service` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (13) definitions
#ASSERT `s 18A(13) "affected employee" the employee is one` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 18A(13) "affected employee" the employee is one` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 18A(13) "affected employee" the employee is one` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- not an employee of the transferor: "means any employee of the transferor".
#ASSERT `s 18A(13) "affected employee" the employee is one` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 18A(13) "trade union" the trade union is one` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 18A(13) "trade union" the trade union is one` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 18A(13) "trade union" the trade union is one` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 18A(13) "transfer" the change of hands is a transfer` `s 18A(13) the disposition of a business as a going concern` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 18A(13) "transfer" the change of hands is a transfer` `s 18A(13) a transfer effected by sale` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 18A(13) "transfer" the change of hands is a transfer` `s 18A(13) a transfer effected by amalgamation` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 18A(13) "transfer" the change of hands is a transfer` `s 18A(13) a transfer effected by merger` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 18A(13) "transfer" the change of hands is a transfer` `s 18A(13) a transfer effected by reconstruction` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 18A(13) "transfer" the change of hands is a transfer` `s 18A(13) a transfer effected by operation of law` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- "includes" opens the list: some other change of hands is not answered.
#ASSERT `s 18A(13) "transfer" the change of hands is a transfer` `s 18A(13) some other change of hands` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 18A(13) "undertaking" the thing is one` `s 18A(13) a trade` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 18A(13) "undertaking" the thing is one` `s 18A(13) a business` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 18A(13) "undertaking" the thing is one` `s 18A(13) something else` EQUALS NOTHING

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§ `s 19 Offence`
#ASSERT `s 19 the employer is guilty of an offence` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 19 the employer is guilty of an offence` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 19 the employer is guilty of an offence` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- No penalty is stated in section 19; the penalty is section 112's (ea2), passed in.  A first conviction and a repeat pick different inputs.
`a first-offence penalty (a made-up fixture, not the Act's)` MEANS `Penalty on conviction` WITH `least fine in dollars` IS 0, `greatest fine in dollars` IS JUST 1000, `longest imprisonment in months` IS NOTHING
`a repeat-offence penalty (a made-up fixture, not the Act's)` MEANS `Penalty on conviction` WITH `least fine in dollars` IS 0, `greatest fine in dollars` IS JUST 2000, `longest imprisonment in months` IS JUST 6
#ASSERT `s 19 the penalty on conviction` (JUST `a first-offence penalty (a made-up fixture, not the Act's)`) (JUST `a repeat-offence penalty (a made-up fixture, not the Act's)`) FALSE EQUALS JUST `a first-offence penalty (a made-up fixture, not the Act's)`
#ASSERT `s 19 the penalty on conviction` (JUST `a first-offence penalty (a made-up fixture, not the Act's)`) (JUST `a repeat-offence penalty (a made-up fixture, not the Act's)`) TRUE EQUALS JUST `a repeat-offence penalty (a made-up fixture, not the Act's)`
-- When section 112 gives none, the penalty is not covered here.
#ASSERT `s 19 the penalty on conviction` NOTHING NOTHING FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Added with the rulings of 2026-11-05 ("if", "where" and scope limits), expected values written from the text of s 18A.
-- s 18A(1)(a): "If an undertaking ... is transferred": no transfer, an unmet "if": no.
#ASSERT `s 18A(1)(a) the contract of service has effect after the transfer as if originally made between the person employed and the transferee` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 18A(2)(c): no completed transfer; a completed transfer but an act of some other kind (scope limit, not covered).
#ASSERT `s 18A(2)(c) the act or omission is deemed to have been done in relation to the transferee` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 18A(2)(c) the act or omission is deemed to have been done in relation to the transferee` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 18A(3): "On the completion of a transfer": not completed; completed but the contract is not preserved (scope limit).
#ASSERT `s 18A(3) the terms and conditions of service are the same as those enjoyed immediately prior to the transfer` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 18A(3) the terms and conditions of service are the same as those enjoyed immediately prior to the transfer` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
